{"id": "EUVD-2026-108717", "enisaUuid": "6e46c437-10a5-3c50-9a3a-4d328f622a34", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ncrypto: ccp - Fix possible deadlock in SEV init failure path\n\n__sev_platform_init_handle_init_ex_path() calls\nrmp_mark_pages_firmware() with locked=false while the parent\nfunction of init_ex_path already acquired the sev_cmd_mutex.\nIn the case of an RMPUPDATE failure for any page after the first, the cleanup\npath would invoke reclaim pages which would result in a deadlock in\nsev_do_cmd.\n\nPass locked=true to honor the lock status of the parent function.", "datePublished": "2026-10-23T11:37:09", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-23T11:37:09", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8e7e06ee7c2938ee3fa31a61cc5289a45c8c13f1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ffd3a3df92be697eb78118a146c6a5d5e6c1f724", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/364f3841bc22c72b6e2cb72a1e3c91c9c8fc1ef4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b0e7ec0dab242c5e480121ba12400d0513e37ca2"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98871"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1d65d524-0eb7-3253-bdf5-a0f76838cf86", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7364a6fbca45f826952ea932699fb2171d06ee73 <8e7e06ee7c2938ee3fa31a61cc5289a45c8c13f1"}, {"id": "4bfe438a-c777-3894-a7f9-730fea17ec13", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "6fdcf866-c80a-30f8-b5d5-6960a8293382", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7364a6fbca45f826952ea932699fb2171d06ee73 <b0e7ec0dab242c5e480121ba12400d0513e37ca2"}, {"id": "79043c4e-2cdf-32e6-bc03-684ef255cc67", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7364a6fbca45f826952ea932699fb2171d06ee73 <364f3841bc22c72b6e2cb72a1e3c91c9c8fc1ef4"}, {"id": "9abc5ac2-27cf-3140-9be8-be03e2362825", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"n